# play logs/control --------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode, mocks: the Logs screen proposed for slice 1, read$
# from a simulated host by the gallery's stand-ins, unit (b)'s$
# to build. It only reads: no plan, no y/N, no journal. No pager$
# runs: an item says what it would run. Nothing on this machine$
# changes: every command and file is the fake's.$
$
# Info: logs/control$
# web-01.example.net runs Debian 13, less installed. Lines hold$
# what commands printed: colour, a title and bell, a bidi$
# override, bytes that are not UTF-8. They show as ^[ and$
# <U+202E> and <0xe9>; origin/main prints them raw to the$
# terminal (logging.go:146; file_logs_repository.go:96;$
# menu/logs_escape.golden).$
$
# Logs #########################################################$
$
# Log ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  File                 /var/log/hardn.log$
   -  Size                 264 bytes, 5 lines$
$
# All 5 lines --------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  2026/10/20 12:00:01 INFO: run 1: $ apt-get update$
   -  2026/10/20 12:00:02 INFO: run 1: | ^[[31mErr:1^[[0m$
      http://deb.example.net$
   -  2026/10/20 12:00:02 INFO: run 1: | ^[]0;a title^Gdone^[[2J$
   -  2026/10/20 12:00:03 INFO: run 2: | abc<U+202E>def$
   -  2026/10/20 12:00:03 INFO: run 2: | caf<0xe9>$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Open                 The whole log in less$
   2) Refresh              Read the log again$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter selection [0-2 or q]: 0$
$
# simulated system ---------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Nothing was applied.$
$

